# Analytical Database Standards

Enforcement: **B**. Do not use warehouses as OLTP systems of record.

## Principles

- Optimize for scan/aggregation patterns; partition and cluster by filter columns that matter.
- Prefer append-only / immutable facts with derived models over row-level mutability.
- Cost control: bound scanned bytes; avoid SELECT * in scheduled jobs.
- Schema evolution via additive columns and versioned models when possible.
- Separate raw, cleaned, and mart layers when the project uses that pattern.

## Anti-patterns

- Point-update heavy workloads on columnar warehouses
- Unpartitioned multi-TB tables queried without filters
- Treating BI extracts as transactional truth
